  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: The RNA branch dominates (0.591 with PCA-2000/multiprofile/avgpool vs 0.208 image-only), and multiprofile avgpool is the best aggregation. The key uncertainty is whether a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) can capture structure that linear PCA-2000 misses, since all RNA results so far use a deterministic linear projection. This experiment (config_005: RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_002, isolating the encoder effect while holding profile, aggregation, and modality fixed. It is the best use of the next budget slot because: (1) the RNA representation is the dominant performance driver, so clarifying whether a learned encoder helps is the highest-impact design question; (2) the answer directly determines which RNA encoder to carry into any future multimodal fusion experiments, preventing wasted budget on suboptimal encoder choices in more complex configurations; (3) it avoids the risk of prematurely investing in multimodal fusion when the image signal is very weak and the RNA branch may still have untapped headroom."
}

